        {
            "block_label": "abstract",
            "block_content": "ABSTRACT. A pole of order  $ m \\in \\mathbb{N} $ at  $ \\beta \\in \\mathbb{C} $ of a regular operator valued function  $ Q : \\mathcal{D}(Q) \\to \\mathcal{L}(\\mathcal{H}) $ is investigated. We provide a characterization of pole cancellation functions  $ \\Psi(z) $ of  $ Q(z) $ of order  $ k \\leq m $ at  $ \\beta $ in terms of the coefficients of the Laurent expansion of  $ Q $. This characterization yields practical and explicit constructions of pole cancellation functions  $ \\Psi(z) $. Moreover, it leads to an explicit formula for the associated functions  $ \\hat{\\Phi}(z) := Q(z) \\Psi(z) $, which are root functions of order  $ k $ at the zero  $ \\beta $ of  $ Q^{-1} $. The results are illustrated by an example.",
            "block_bbox": [
                304,
                443,
                887,
                620
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    304.0,
                    443.0
                ],
                [
                    887.0,
                    443.0
                ],
                [
                    887.0,
                    620.0
                ],
                [
                    304.0,
                    620.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "### 1. INTRODUCTION",
            "block_bbox": [
                504,
                696,
                689,
                718
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
